These statements look like a lobbying strategy. Advisers in Washington (aka Khalilzad and his likes) may urged the Taliban to talk about investment and girls’ education so they can keep power and look legitimate.

Americans should not forget the U.S. soldiers killed by the Taliban. They should also reject another deal like the Doha Agreement. 

The Taliban are terrorists, not partners of the free world. They are stalling so terror can take hold in Afghanistan and later threaten the West. As President Bush put it: fool me once (Doha agreement), shame on you; fool me twice, shame on me!

